8. Analytics
Two independent systems:
A) Custom business analytics (what visitors do on the site)
Logging endpoints: `app/api/track/click/route.ts` and `app/api/track/search/route.ts`. Anonymous, region-stamped, fire-and-forget (always return 200 so they never block the user). Region comes from `x-vercel-ip-country` header or the request body.
Wired in: `ConciergeThread.tsx` pings `/api/track/click` on a partner tap (with `keepalive`); `HomeApp.tsx` `runQuery` pings `/api/track/search` on a search.
Viewed at `/admin/stats`: top partners by clicks, clicks by region, top searches, searches by region, and unmet demand (searches that returned 0 results = opportunities for new partners).
B) Vercel Web Analytics (traffic counts)
Enabled in the Vercel dashboard (free tier) + `<Analytics />` from `@vercel/analytics/react` is rendered in `app/layout.tsx`.
Shows visitors, page views, top pages, countries — in the Vercel dashboard's Analytics tab.
Privacy note: all analytics are anonymous aggregates. The site never identifies individual anonymous visitors (not possible/legal). Logged-in users are known only because they chose to sign up.
Where the money/sales data lives
Actual commissions/sales are NOT in this app — they're in the affiliate network dashboards (Awin, Admitad, Travelpayouts, Amazon). The site only tracks clicks/searches; the networks credit and pay the sales. Payouts are configured per-network (bank/PayPal) in each network's own dashboard.
